course: dictionary
lesson: 2963
title: Tiny drops
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A droplet is a very small drop of liquid. The ending -let is a clue, because it often means small, as in booklet or piglet. So a droplet is a little drop of water, or another liquid.
explain: Read the words around it. «Clouds form when moist air rises and cools; when the droplets grow heavy they fall as rain.» Grow heavy and fall tell you that droplets are tiny pieces of water that float in the air and join together until they are heavy enough to fall.
explain: Droplets show up in many places. «Breathed-out air is warm and full of water vapour, which turns into tiny droplets of mist on cold glass.» Tiny droplets is a phrase you will meet often in science, and tiny helps you see that the drops are very small.
explain: Be careful: the steam is not the droplets. «Steam is invisible: the white cloud above a kettle is tiny droplets.» The steam itself is a gas that you cannot see, but the droplets that form when it cools are the white cloud you can see.
fact: A droplet is a very small drop of liquid.
fact: The plural of droplet is droplets: one droplet, many droplets.
fact: Clouds are made of tiny water droplets floating in the air.
fact: Dew forms droplets on grass, and condensation makes droplets on a cold window.
fact: A cough or sneeze can spread germs in droplets, so catch it, bin it, kill it, and cover your mouth.
exercise: «Breathed-out air turns into tiny droplets of mist on cold glass.» What is a droplet? | A kind of gas you cannot see | A hard, dry piece of ice | A very large, heavy cloud | *A very small drop of liquid
exercise: The ending -let in droplet is a clue. What does it often mean? | Wet all over | *Small | Very fast | Far away
exercise: Copy the word that means tiny drops in «Shake a bottle of salad dressing and the oil breaks into tiny droplets for a while.» | breaks | *droplets | salad | bottle
test: Which thing in the sky is made of tiny water droplets? | *Clouds | Stars | Thunder | Lightning
test: «Air conditioners drip water outside because cooling the air turns water vapour into droplets.» What does cooling water vapour turn it into? | Dry sand | Warm air | *Droplets | Heavy stones
exam: Which phrase best describes a droplet of dew on grass? | *A tiny drop of liquid | A huge puddle | A flash of light | A dry crumb
